SWEET CHG MON AFTER A REFUSED P3 (patch 0339, ALL-ON T-58): a refused P3 (patch 0287 p3_refuse, e.g. 'CNFG_09 ILIM is already 875 mA or more' when the charger chip keeps the previous boot's raise across the SoC reset) ended the 30 s SWEET CHG MON rows too, so the boot had no temp= row at all (patch 0307 prints temp only there) and the host safety monitor (docs/SAFETY-CHECKLIST.md S1/S3) cut it as hot at 480 s [obs boot resident-052305-b1, job 20261113T052231Z-tools-4422, kernel allon-trunk1: 'P3 refused ... already 875 mA', 0 MON rows, 'SAFETY FAIL S3']. Now a refused P3 with a live bus enters stage 10: one MON row (mon_row of 0298/0307, unchanged) every P3_SAMPLE_MS (30 s), the first at the next tick, behind the same phase-1 gate i2c_gate(0) the stage-3 watcher checks first; a lost gate or a failed read ends the rows with a GAP. READS ONLY: the same four fuel-gauge registers (0x36: 0x0a, 0x09, 0x06, 0x08) and the existing per-transfer controller path; no chip write (stage 10 calls no writer: mon_row and i2c_gate only read or set per-transfer controller registers; i2c_cnfg09_write has no stage check, its callers p3_step (stage 1, never re-entered), p3_step500, p3_lost and the 0336 hold/release (needs p3_nwrites == 1, stays 0) are not reached; host case mr_zero_chip_writes: 0 writes over 700 s), no new register. p3_stage >= 9 keeps meaning 'P3 ended' for patch 0336 (thermal hold/release stay 'nothing to do' on such a boot: tracker T-58 D2). Applies after 0336.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_chg_i2c.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_chg_i2c.c
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_chg_i2c.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_chg_i2c.c
@@ -783,9 +783,45 @@
 {
 	i2c_log("SWEET CHG GAP: P3 refused, CNFG_09 not written: %s\n", why);
 	p3_done("refused");
+	/*
+	 * Patch 0339 (ALL-ON T-58): a refused P3 used to end the battery rows too: no SWEET CHG MON row (the only temp= source of patch 0307) for the whole boot, so the host
+	 * safety monitor (S1 hot / S3 no temp row, docs/SAFETY-CHECKLIST.md) ran blind and cut the boot at 480 s [obs resident-052305-b1: the chip kept CNFG_09 ILIM=900 mA
+	 * from the previous boot -> 'ILIM is already 875 mA or more']. The MON row (patch 0298/0307) is reads only (fuel gauge 0x36: 0x0a, 0x09, 0x06, 0x08); stage 10 runs
+	 * only it, every P3_SAMPLE_MS, behind the same phase-1 gate the stage-3 watcher checks first. No chip write: stage 10 calls no writer (i2c_cnfg09_write has no stage
+	 * check; its callers p3_step = stage 1 only, p3_step500, p3_lost, 0336 hold/release = p3_nwrites 1 only, are not reached). p3_stage >= 9 keeps meaning "P3 ended" for 0336.
+	 */
+	if (!i2c_dead) {
+		p3_stage = 10;
+		p3_t0_ms = i2c_now_ms();
+		p3_next_ms = p3_t0_ms;          /* first row at the next tick: the host gets a temp= row seconds after the refusal */
+		i2c_log("SWEET CHG MON: P3 refused, battery rows go on every %u s (patch 0339, reads only, no CNFG_09 write)\n", P3_SAMPLE_MS / 1000u);
+	}
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void mon_row(uint32_t t_s);      /* patch 0339: defined below (patch 0298) */
+
+/* Patch 0339: stage 10 = battery rows only after a refused P3 (see p3_refuse). A lost gate or a failed read ends the rows with a GAP (never a silent stop). */
+static void
+p3_mon_only_tick(void)
+{
+	if (i2c_now_ms() < p3_next_ms) {
+		return;
+	}
+	if (i2c_dead || !i2c_gate(0)) {
+		(void)i2c_wr(I_INTEN, 0);
+		i2c_log("SWEET CHG GAP: MON rows after a refused P3 stop (%s): no more battery rows this boot\n", i2c_dead ? "bus stopped" : "phase-1 gate lost");
+		p3_stage = 9;
+		return;
+	}
+	mon_row((uint32_t)((p3_next_ms - p3_t0_ms) / 1000u));
+	if (i2c_dead) {
+		p3_stage = 9;           /* mon_row logged the GAP that names the fuel gauge */
+		return;
+	}
+	p3_next_ms += P3_SAMPLE_MS;
+}
+
 /* Write val to CNFG_09 (via the guarded writer), read it back, log before/after. Returns 1 when the read-back equals val. */
 static int
 p3_write_verify(uint8_t cur, uint8_t val, uint8_t *readback)
@@ -1146,6 +1182,10 @@
